# M1_HH.ode -- isochrons by BRUTE FORCE (method M1), reduced Hodgkin-Huxley neuron (Osinga & Moehlis 2010, eq. 4.1)
#
# ======================================================================================
# WHAT TO DO IN THE XPPAUT WINDOW   (or run M1_HH.xps: File > Do script, which does
#                                    all of it; XPPAUT 8.4 or XPPAUT-Web)
# ======================================================================================
#  A. The phase map, coloured (every dot = one starting point, colour = its phase)
#   1. Viewaxes > 2D: X-axis vs, Y-axis ns, Xlabel v, Ylabel n           (keys v 2)
#   2. nUmerics > Color code > Another quantity:  theta,  Choose,  Min 0,  Max 1
#      (keys u c a), then Esc back to the main menu
#   3. Initialconds > 2par range                                              (keys i 2)
#        Vary1 vs    Start1 -90   End1 52
#        Vary2 ns    Start2 0.3   End2 0.8
#        Steps 70    Steps2 70    Crv(1) Array(2): 2
#        Reset storage: N   (keep every run: one dot each)
#        Use old ic's: Y    (every run starts from its own point; with N each run
#                            would go on from where the last one ended)
#        Cycle color: N   Movie: N
#      Ok.  4900 runs; each leaves one dot at its starting point, coloured by its
#      phase.  The picture is the PHASE MAP: the colour bands are the isochrons.
#   4. Nullcline > New (keys n n): the nullclines on top; they cross at the equilibrium
#      x* inside the cycle, where all the colours meet.
#
#  B. Isochrons as dots, in a second window (the same runs, nothing to compute again)
#   5. Makewindow > Create (keys m c): a new window, which is now the active one.
#      First repeat step 2 in it (a new window copies the colour settings but not the
#      quantity; without this, XPP also redraws window 1 with the wrong colours)
#   6. nUmerics > Color code > No color (keys u c n), Esc
#   7. Viewaxes > 2D: X-axis vb, Y-axis nb, Xlabel v, Ylabel n
#      (and the same window), then Restore (keys r): only the starting points whose
#      phase is within dth of 0, 1/niso, 2/niso, ... are left: niso isochrons.
#   8. Nullcline > New (keys n n) in this window too.
#      (niso, dth: Param window, then run 3 again.)
#
#  C. One point:  ICs vs=-50, ns=0.55;  Viewaxes > 2D: t, theta;  Initialconds
#      > Go: theta jumps to its final value after the first spike (here 0.269).
#
# ======================================================================================
# THE METHOD (M1, brute force)
# ======================================================================================
#  Ingredients (computed once, numbers below):  the limit cycle Γ, its period T, a phase
#  zero gamma0 on Γ (the point of Γ with the largest v), and a spike threshold thr.
#
#  For every starting point x0 on a grid:
#   step 1  integrate x0 for a time trans, long enough to settle onto Γ
#           (Γ attracts by about 10^20 per period)
#   step 2  record s = the time of an upward crossing of v = thr after settling
#   step 3  the same crossing for the cycle itself: starting at gamma0, Γ first crosses
#           thr upward at t = tc0.  x0 is then late by (s - tc0) compared with gamma0,
#           so its ASYMPTOTIC PHASE (clock reading) is
#                theta(x0) = (tc0 - s)/T   mod 1
#   step 4  the isochron of phase th = the set of grid points with theta = th:
#           the colour bands (window 1), or the points within dth of th (window 2)
#
#  Why it works: x0 and the point of Γ with phase theta(x0) approach each other, so they
#  cross thr at the same times once x0 has settled.  Only forward integration is needed.
#  What it costs: one full integration per grid point; the grid sets the resolution.
#  Its limitation: see M1_limitation_slowmanifold_HH.ode.  Osinga & Moehlis (2010)
#  show that all isochrons come exponentially close to the repelling slow manifold (an
#  "almost phaseless set") and arbitrarily close to the equilibrium x* = (-59.6044, 0.402577)
#  (the phaseless set); across such thin layers a grid cannot resolve the phase.
#
#  How this file is laid out (XPP draws nullclines only when the plot axes are variables):
#   (vs, ns)  the starting point, as variables that barely move (their equations are
#              eps times the model's, eps = 1e-9): 2par range varies their initial values,
#              window 1 plots them, and their nullclines are the model's nullclines
#   (vb, nb)  the same again, for window 2; a point whose phase is not near k/niso is
#              moved down off the picture at its first spike after settling
#   (V, N)    the trajectory itself, started from (vs, ns) at t = 1e-6
# ======================================================================================

# --- the model: the reduced Hodgkin-Huxley neuron of Osinga & Moehlis (2010), eq. (4.1):
#     m = minf(v) (fast), h = 0.8 - n;  I = 10 (repetitive firing)
am(x)=0.1*(x+40)/(1-exp(-(x+40)/10))
bm(x)=4*exp(-(x+65)/18)
an(x)=0.01*(x+55)/(1-exp(-(x+55)/10))
bn(x)=0.125*exp(-(x+65)/80)
minf(x)=am(x)/(am(x)+bm(x))
fx(x,y)=iapp-gna*minf(x)^3*(0.8-y)*(x-ena)-gk*y^4*(x-ek)-gl*(x-el)
fy(x,y)=an(x)*(1-y)-bn(x)*y
par iapp=10,gna=120,gk=36,gl=0.3,ena=50,ek=-77,el=-54.4

# --- the ingredients: Γ has period per; it crosses v = thr upward for the first time
#     tc0 after gamma0 = (44.706379, 0.45973791), the point of Γ with the largest v
par per=11.84628522, thr=-20, tc0=11.74002818

# --- step 1: the starting point x0 = (vs, ns) (and its copy (vb, nb) for window 2)
par eps=1e-9
vs'=eps*fx(vs,ns)
ns'=eps*fy(vs,ns)
vb'=eps*fx(vb,nb)
nb'=eps*fy(vb,nb)
init vs=-50,ns=0.55,vb=-50,nb=0.55
#     the trajectory from x0: it starts at x0 at t = 1e-6
V'=fx(V,N)
N'=fy(V,N)
init V=-50,N=0.55
global 1 t-1e-6 {V=vs;N=ns;vb=vs;nb=ns}

# --- step 2 and step 3: at every upward crossing of v = thr (time t = s), the asymptotic
#     phase theta = (tc0 - s)/T mod 1 (theta stays -1 until the first spike, e.g. for a
#     start at the equilibrium).  Window 2: at a crossing after settling (t > tset), a
#     point whose phase is farther than dth from every multiple of 1/niso is moved down
#     off the picture.
par niso=10, dth=0.012, tset=56.8622
theta'=0
init theta=-1
global 1 V-thr {theta=mod((tc0-t)/per,1);nb=if((t>tset)*(abs(mod(mod((tc0-t)/per,1)*niso+0.5,1)-0.5)>(dth*niso)))then(nb-10)else(nb)}

# --- numerics: settle for 6 periods, then store the last 1.3 periods (every 100th step)
@ meth=rk4, dt=0.01, trans=71.0777, total=86.4779, nout=100, bound=1e6, maxstor=1000000
#     every run of a range starts again from its own point ("Use old ic's" = Y, XPP's
#     default; with N each run would go on from where the last one ended)
@ rangereset=no, rangeoldic=yes
@ xp=vs, yp=ns, xlo=-90, xhi=52, ylo=0.3, yhi=0.8, lt=-3, colormap=1, nmesh=200
done
